cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CogWAM: Cognitive World-Action Model with Event-Driven Semantic Memory"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: The CogWAM Authors
abstract: >-
  CogWAM couples a vision-language backbone to a dual-width mixture-of-transformers
  that jointly denoises a future visual latent and an action chunk, conditioned on
  an event-driven semantic memory that is refreshed by an explicit KEEP/UPDATE
  decision rather than on every step.
keywords:
  - vision-language-action
  - world-model
  - robot-learning
  - semantic-memory
  - robodojo
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: software
    title: "StarVLA: A Lego-like Codebase for Vision-Language-Action Model Developing"
    authors:
      - name: starVLA Community
    repository-code: "https://github.com/starVLA/starVLA"
    license: MIT
    notes: CogWAM is derived from the StarVLA codebase.
  - type: software
    title: "RoboDojo: a robot simulation benchmark"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/RoboDojo-Benchmark/RoboDojo"
    version: 0.2.0
    notes: Evaluation benchmark used for all reported numbers.
